[[File:Palazzo bernardo nani gran canal dorsoduro.jpg|thumb|Palazzo Bernardo Nani]]
The '''Palazzo Bernardo Nani Lucheschi''', also called the '''Palazzo Nani Bernardo''', is a [[Renaissance architecture|Renaissance]]-style palace between the {{ill|Ca' Bernardo (Dorsoduro)|lt=Palazzo Giustinian Bernardo|it}} and the larger and more grandiose [[Ca' Rezzonico]], on the [[Grand Canal of Venice|Grand Canal]] in the [[sestiere of Dorsoduro]] in [[Venice]], Italy.

==History==
The building was built in the mid-16th century at the site of an earlier palace, commissioned by the patrician Bernardo family from [[Alessandro Vittoria]]. Originally, the main facade of the palace faced the site of the Ca' Rezzonico, formerly a garden. That facade was once heavily frescoed. The canal facade was added in the 17th century. The palace is privately owned and rented for events or as apartments.<ref>[https://www.palazzonanibernardo.it Official site] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140206013110/http://www.palazzonanibernardo.it/index.asp |date=2014-02-06 }}</ref>

